# What must never reach a deployed image.
#
# There was no such file, so `COPY . .` shipped everything in this directory:
# two database dumps, the live development SQLite database with real rows in it,
# a 145 MB Windows virtualenv that cannot run on Linux anyway, and the owner's
# private tools. A deployed container held a user's email address and an
# encrypted Shopify token for no reason at all.

# Data. None of it belongs anywhere near a running service.
*.bak
*.dump
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
aco_dev*

# Secrets. The orchestrator supplies these; a stray copy in the image would
# quietly answer for them instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Built on the host, for the host. The image installs its own.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The owner's own scripts, deliberately outside the repository. Nothing in the
# application imports them, so nothing needs them at runtime.
tools/
